{"id":"akzent","lemma":"Akzent","pos":"noun","rank":2742,"glosses":["accent (modulation of the voice)","accent (stress mark)"],"ipa":"/akˈt͡sɛnt/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/be/De-Akzent.ogg/De-Akzent.ogg.mp3","gender":"m","forms":{"genitive":"Akzentes","plural":"Akzente"},"examples":[{"text":"Ich liebe deinen Akzent.","en":"I love your accent.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"lovable","l":"lieb"},{"g":"thy, your .","l":"dein"},null]},{"text":"Jeder hat einen Akzent.","en":"Everyone has an accent.","words":[{"g":"each"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"a","l":"ein"},null]},{"text":"Er spricht Englisch mit einem deutschen Akzent.","en":"He speaks English with a German accent.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to speak","l":"sprechen"},{"g":"A children’s game for…"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"(to) a","l":"ein"},{"g":"German","l":"deutsch"},null]},{"text":"Er machte sich über meinen Akzent lustig.","en":"He made fun of my accent.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to make","l":"machen"},{"g":"oneself"},{"g":"[with accusative or…"},{"g":"to opine, to think"},null,{"g":"funny, humorous"}]},{"text":"Tom spricht ohne Akzent.","en":"Tom speaks without an accent.","words":[null,{"g":"to speak","l":"sprechen"},{"g":"without"},null]}]}